    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d142">

                <pb facs="0187" n="177" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg177"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/12–3044: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-29T00:00:00-04:00">January 29,
                            1945—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>712. (SCOFM<anchor n="42" xml:id="d142-f1"/>) Your 11575 December 30.<anchor
                        n="43" xml:id="d142-f2"/> Please inform your colleagues on the European
                    Advisory Commission that this Government <pb facs="0188" n="178" xml:id="pg178"
                    /> is very glad to give its approval in principle to the five proposals advanced
                    by the French representative, the general aim of which is to place the French in
                    a position of equality with the United States, United Kingdom and Soviet Union
                    in handling German matters. It is our understanding that you will concert with
                    the Soviet representative in bringing our views formally to the attention of the
                    Commission.</p>
                <p>It will be desirable from the standpoint of planning for the military occupation
                    of Germany if French participation will not operate to disturb unduly agreements
                    already reached on a tripartite basis or to result in major revision of policy
                    decisions already reached.</p>
                <p>Please inform Murphy.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d142-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent to London. Repeated to Paris and Moscow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d142-f1" n="42" xml:id="d142-f1-content">
                <p>Secret for the Chief of Mission</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d142-f2" n="43" xml:id="d142-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; it outlined the contents of a memorandum circulated in the European
                    Advisory Commission by the French Representative. For text of memorandum, see
                        <ref target="frus1944v01#pg_427">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1944, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 427</ref>
                </p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d142-f3" n="44" xml:id="d142-f3-content">
                <p>Robert D. Murphy, United States Political Adviser for Germany</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
